\label{def:gd}
    Fix dataset size $n$. We say model $F(X,\theta)$ has Good Properties if, with a considerably small constant $C>0$ and $B := \max\{O(\sqrt{\log(Nmd/\delta)}), 1\}$:
    \begin{multicols}{3}
        \begin{enumerate}
        \item $\omega = \Theta(\frac{1}{N L^2d^{2.5}B^3})$;
        \item $\kappa = \frac{1}{\sqrt{m}}$;
        \item $m = \Omega(\frac{n^3L^5\exp(Cd)}{\omega^6\lambda^6\delta^3 N^{2}})$.
        \end{enumerate}
    \end{multicols}
    The Good Model Class is ${\cal F}_{\sf M, T, N}(\mathbb{D}):= \{F(\cdot, \theta({\sf T})) : \theta(0) \sim \mathcal{N}(0, I_{\sf M}), \theta({\sf T}) \in {\cal A}_{{\sf T},{\sf N}}(\theta(0), \mathbb{D})\}$ with $|\mathbb{D}|={\sf N}$.

\label{lem:perturbations:informal}
