\label{thm:lower_stat:informal}
    Fix a non-trivial subspace ${\cal H}^*\subseteq{\cal H}_K$ of the RKHS associated with the layer-wise NTKs. There exists a family of target functions $\{F_\theta^*\}_{\theta\in\Theta_{\sf N}}\subset {\cal H}^*$ and a constant $c>0$ such that for any (possibly randomized) estimator $\widehat F$ measurable with respect to $\mathbb{D}\sim {\cal D}^{\otimes {\sf N}}$:
    \begin{align*}
        \sup_{F^*\in\{F_\theta^*\}_{\theta\in\Theta_{\sf N}}}{\mathbb{E}}_{\mathbb{D}}\big[\Delta{\cal R}(\widehat F)\big] \ge c \cdot \frac{\xi^2}{{\sf N}}.
    \end{align*}
    In particular, the upper bound $O(\xi^2/{\sf N})$ in Theorem~\ref{thm:generalization:informal} is tight up to a constant.

